    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0214" n="98" xml:id="pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/98.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Chinese Government obliged to seek abroad for funds for the Hwai River project.
                    It invites American capital and would probably give an option of one year to
                    Americans to raise loan and make contract for construction. The necessity for
                    the work for the safety and well-fare of millions and its soundness as a
                    business investment undoubted. Mr. Jameson will proceed to the United States
                    with engineering plans to assist in making arrangements for capital if the Red
                    Cross is willing to continue support to the extent of endeavoring to interest
                    American financiers and industrials in the taking up this work. Please
                    instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
